From: canoziia <canoziia@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] router: stream the PD prefill hop and forward its SSE keep-alive comments

For a `stream: true` client the prefill hop is now requested as a stream
too (max_tokens=1, stream_options.include_usage for 0001's usage merge;
the Responses API reports usage in response.completed). The router adds
no keep-alive timer of its own: it is a shell around the engines, and
whether keep-alive comments are sent is decided by the engines' own vLLM
--sse-keep-alive-interval (vllm-project/vllm#51034).

  * the prefill hop's HTTP status is known before the client's response
    starts; a >=400 status and its body are passed through as-is, like a
    direct call to vLLM;
  * after the prefill hop's 200 the client's StreamingResponse starts;
    SSE comment events (lines starting with ':') are forwarded verbatim,
    the 1-token data events and [DONE] are dropped and only the usage is
    kept; an error event is forwarded (followed by [DONE]) and ends the
    stream; then the decode stream follows unchanged (its comments too);
  * a client disconnect cancels the generator, which closes the prefill
    or decode socket so the engine aborts the request (logged);
  * prompt_tokens_details.multimodal_tokens (null), which the streaming
    usage omits, is restored so router_hops stays byte-identical.

Non-streaming requests are unchanged.
